From 3a0945ac4b15576e84642e9eec4b88ca873c2c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bitranox <rnowotny1966@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 23:55:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: x86: forward HvCallRetargetDeviceInterrupt to userspace

kvm_hv_hypercall() completes every hypercall it does not itself implement
with HV_STATUS_INVALID_HYPERCALL_CODE and does not exit to userspace. That
includes HVCALL_RETARGET_INTERRUPT (0x7e), which a guest issues to move a
VPCI device's MSI/MSI-X interrupt to a different target processor set.

The interrupt routing table for such a device lives in the userspace VMM,
not in KVM, so KVM cannot service the call in-kernel. A guest that drives
Hyper-V VPCI passthrough (for example Linux hv_pci) then fails every
IRQ-affinity change with "irq_retarget_interrupt() failed: 0x2".

Forward HVCALL_RETARGET_INTERRUPT to userspace, the same way POST_MESSAGE
and SIGNAL_EVENT are forwarded. The input is a memory structure at ingpa,
so reject the register-only (fast) form.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: bitranox <rnowotny1966@gmail.com>
---
 arch/x86/kvm/hyperv.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/hyperv.c b/arch/x86/kvm/hyperv.c
index fd4eb1e561f7f..85fed81f81d9f 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/hyperv.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/hyperv.c
@@ -2681,6 +2681,19 @@ int kvm_hv_hypercall(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 			break;
 		}
 		goto hypercall_userspace_exit;
+	case HVCALL_RETARGET_INTERRUPT:
+		/*
+		 * Retarget a VPCI device interrupt (an MSI/MSI-X affinity change).
+		 * The device's interrupt routing table lives in the userspace VMM,
+		 * not in KVM, so forward the call there.  The input is a memory
+		 * structure at ingpa; the register-only (fast) form is not defined
+		 * for it, so reject that.
+		 */
+		if (unlikely(hc.fast)) {
+			ret = HV_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+			break;
+		}
+		goto hypercall_userspace_exit;
 	default:
 		ret = HV_STATUS_INVALID_HYPERCALL_CODE;
 		break;
-- 
